1
00:00:09,060 --> 00:00:13,380
Brighten up the peace and try to step away.

2
00:00:17,840 --> 00:00:22,797
Hello,

3
00:00:22,847 --> 00:00:27,020
goodbye.

4
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:31,500
The one who goes home as
soon as the night is over.

5
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:39,820
Chuwappa!

6
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:49,360
Don't rush in this narrow town. Haste makes waste,
so take the long way round.

7
00:00:49,900 --> 00:01:03,000
If by any chance there's someone better than me, tell me.
Tell me all night long.

8
00:01:04,240 --> 00:01:08,360
Chuwappa, black shwaa, la la la la la la.

9
00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:17,000
I don't mind waiting,
because I'm a Kameza woman.

10
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:21,660
I don't want to lose, Ginza woman.

11
00:01:21,660 --> 00:01:30,000
I'll love you for years,
on the path of the Kameza woman.

12
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:42,020
Violent crime is skyrocketing.

13
00:01:42,020 --> 00:01:46,060
New types of crime involving
computers and the like are emerging.

14
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:49,480
Juvenile crime is involving
ever younger offenders.

15
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:54,600
But the number of police officers needed
to deal with these is clearly insufficient.

16
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:59,080
But headquarters anticipated
today's situation long ago,

17
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:02,060
and has been preparing countermeasures.

18
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:03,980
Ohara.

19
00:02:03,980 --> 00:02:05,760
Yes, sir!

20
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:13,380
This is the ultimate police officer, built
over 30 years with a 5 billion yen budget.

21
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:15,740
Dispatch!

22
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:17,160
Robot police officer.

23
00:02:19,860 --> 00:02:22,280
What? A robot cop is coming?

24
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:22,880
Yes.

25
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:26,860
Apparently the Chief and Terai
are heading over here together now.

26
00:02:26,860 --> 00:02:31,420
Don't tell me it's going to turn
out to be some cop named Mr. Robot.

27
00:02:32,060 --> 00:02:34,480
No, it really is a robot, apparently.

28
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:39,300
I hear it was developed over 30
years with a 5 billion yen budget.

29
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:41,540
I'm looking forward to seeing
what kind of robot shows up.

30
00:02:41,540 --> 00:02:42,020
Yeah.

31
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:44,440
I have a bad feeling about this.

32
00:02:44,440 --> 00:02:46,360
It cost 5 billion yen, you know.

33
00:02:46,820 --> 00:02:49,340
There's no way some weird
robot is coming, right?

34
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:52,040
Exactly, Ryo-chan, you're overthinking it.

35
00:02:52,040 --> 00:02:55,640
Naive! It's a robot the higher-ups
at headquarters came up with!

36
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:58,460
Do you really think it'll be
something like what we're hoping for?

37
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:00,640
Considering the ages of those higher-ups...

38
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:04,080
It might be a robot that looks like
a kettle stuck on top of an oil drum.

39
00:03:05,760 --> 00:03:08,340
But it might surprisingly be a giant robot.

40
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,700
Maybe it transforms from
a vehicle or something.

41
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:19,500
A robot cop like that would be fun,
wouldn't it?

42
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:22,080
Why are you imagining
something so elaborate?

43
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:25,520
Well, no matter what kind of robot shows up,
it wouldn't be surprising.

44
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:28,100
After all, it was made by people like us.

45
00:03:28,100 --> 00:03:28,880
Here it comes.

46
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:31,840
Hey, everyone, sorry to keep you waiting.

47
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:38,920
This is Robot Police Officer 001, which took
30 years and a 5 billion yen budget to build.

48
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:40,560
Aw, I knew it.

49
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:41,740
So that's how it is

50
00:03:41,740 --> 00:03:44,080
Then go ahead and transform it right away.

51
00:03:44,080 --> 00:03:45,600
W-what are you talking about?

52
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:48,620
This car transforms into
the robot cop, right?

53
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:51,260
What nonsense are you talking about?

54
00:03:51,260 --> 00:03:52,820
Hey, bring up the data.

55
00:03:52,820 --> 00:03:53,320
Yes.

56
00:04:01,220 --> 00:04:04,500
Well, surprised?
It's exactly like a real human, right?

57
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:07,000
What part of this is exactly like a human?

58
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:09,860
Anyone can see it's obviously fake.

59
00:04:10,580 --> 00:04:12,020
Don't be rude.

60
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:17,840
The 001 was built by pouring in 30
years and a 5 billion yen budget!

61
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:23,580
You can say that because you
haven't seen the 001 in action.

62
00:04:23,580 --> 00:04:25,940
Alright, let's get it moving, then.

63
00:04:25,940 --> 00:04:27,840
Terai, get it moving.

64
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:29,600
Excuse me, Ryo-san.

65
00:04:31,460 --> 00:04:34,120
Whoa, how many dozens of switches
did they put on this thing?

66
00:04:34,780 --> 00:04:38,340
If you kick it really hard in the crotch,
it'll shut down, right?

67
00:04:38,340 --> 00:04:39,820
Just like us, then.

68
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:45,060
It's a robot built over 30
years with a 5 billion yen budget!

69
00:04:45,060 --> 00:04:49,440
Having human-like quirks like that makes it more charming,
doesn't it?

70
00:04:49,440 --> 00:04:50,880
Is that how it is?

71
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:52,120
That's how it is.

72
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:52,820
Chief.

73
00:04:54,840 --> 00:04:56,980
Let's just get it inside for now.

74
00:04:56,980 --> 00:04:57,940
Y-yes, sir.

75
00:04:59,460 --> 00:05:01,340
Now then, let's activate it properly.

76
00:05:01,340 --> 00:05:01,840
Yes.

77
00:05:05,080 --> 00:05:05,960
Hello, everyone.

78
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:07,420
I-it talked!

79
00:05:07,940 --> 00:05:11,540
I am Robot Police Officer 001.

80
00:05:11,540 --> 00:05:14,540
Did you hear that?
It actually spoke proper Japanese!

81
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:16,000
Surprised, right?

82
00:05:16,460 --> 00:05:18,380
It's not really that surprising.

83
00:05:18,380 --> 00:05:20,700
Even computers talk these days, you know.

84
00:05:20,700 --> 00:05:22,480
And far more fluently than that.

85
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:26,860
A robot built over 30 years
with a 5 billion yen budget -

86
00:05:26,860 --> 00:05:29,020
Don't lump it together
with some ordinary computer.

87
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:32,440
Don't mind what he says.

88
00:05:32,440 --> 00:05:34,780
I welcome you.

89
00:05:36,020 --> 00:05:39,560
Chief, if you want to shake hands,
you should just say so.

90
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:40,640
I see.

91
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:42,540
You don't respond to favors,
do you, you bastard.

92
00:05:42,540 --> 00:05:43,320
Shut up.

93
00:05:46,060 --> 00:05:47,680
Let's shake hands, Unit 001.

94
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:48,200
Yes.

95
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:56,120
Since things have turned out this way,

96
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:58,100
I'll be taking a leave
of absence for a while,

97
00:05:58,100 --> 00:06:01,500
so look after Unit 001
for me while I'm gone.

98
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:01,960
Yes.

99
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:03,160
Especially you, Ryotsu.

100
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:05,540
If 001 gets broken or damaged,

101
00:06:05,540 --> 00:06:07,240
you'll be the one paying for it, understand?

102
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:08,540
Why me?

103
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:11,080
Who else would break it but you?

104
00:06:11,460 --> 00:06:14,520
Headquarters spent 30 years on Unit 001,

105
00:06:16,060 --> 00:06:17,380
Headquarters developed it, right?

106
00:06:18,300 --> 00:06:20,760
Y-yeah. Handle it with care, got it?

107
00:06:20,820 --> 00:06:21,960
Got it.

108
00:06:22,220 --> 00:06:22,920
I'm counting on you.

109
00:06:24,020 --> 00:06:25,400
What do we do, senior?

110
00:06:25,640 --> 00:06:29,680
If we mess with it and something goes wrong, the Chief will nag us about it.
Let's just leave it alone.

111
00:06:29,960 --> 00:06:32,860
Isn't this 001 in the way
in the middle of the room?

112
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:35,145
Yeah, you're right. Hey,

113
00:06:35,195 --> 00:06:37,720
001, go to the corner of the room.

114
00:06:38,020 --> 00:06:38,980
Understood.

115
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:46,820
Okay, just stand there for a while.

116
00:06:46,820 --> 00:06:47,820
Understood.

117
00:06:48,480 --> 00:06:50,700
Now we can focus on this in peace.

118
00:07:16,220 --> 00:07:17,720
Ryo-san, what's wrong?

119
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:20,220
Don't just stand there staring at me.

120
00:07:20,840 --> 00:07:23,100
I haven't been doing anything of the sort.

121
00:07:23,100 --> 00:07:25,420
It only feels that way to you, senpai.

122
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:26,980
Because it isn't moving at all.

123
00:07:26,980 --> 00:07:27,880
Is that so?

124
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:29,640
Speaking of which,

125
00:07:30,100 --> 00:07:33,500
those police mannequins we used to see along the roads were creepy too,
weren't they.

126
00:07:33,500 --> 00:07:36,240
So this one feels that
way for the same reason.

127
00:07:36,700 --> 00:07:37,760
Alright, 0015.

128
00:07:38,980 --> 00:07:39,280
Face that way.

129
00:07:39,280 --> 00:07:41,480
Which way is "that way," exactly?

130
00:07:41,480 --> 00:07:44,620
It means turn right
about and face the window.

131
00:07:44,620 --> 00:07:45,380
Roger that.

132
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:50,700
Alright, now we can finally
get some work done in peace.

133
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:10,720
I told you not to look, didn't I?
Don't look!

134
00:08:11,020 --> 00:08:12,440
I wasn't really looking.

135
00:08:12,620 --> 00:08:15,460
Hey, forget it.
Just go out on patrol somewhere!

136
00:08:15,780 --> 00:08:17,200
Somewhere? Where exactly?

137
00:08:19,620 --> 00:08:23,240
No good, Ryo-chan. He won't move
unless you give him specific orders.

138
00:08:23,620 --> 00:08:25,411
Ugh, what a pain. Fine,

139
00:08:25,461 --> 00:08:28,880
go from Kanna Nana onto the old
Mito Highway and make a full loop.

140
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:30,080
Understood.

141
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:37,100
W-what?

142
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:39,240
Where's Kanna Nana?

143
00:08:40,040 --> 00:08:42,552
If you don't know, just say so. Honestly,

144
00:08:42,602 --> 00:08:44,760
you should have at least
loaded the map software into it.

145
00:08:45,140 --> 00:08:48,147
Senpai,
there's a map CD-ROM in the cupboard,

146
00:08:48,197 --> 00:08:49,660
so let's install it.

147
00:08:50,060 --> 00:08:51,100
Yeah, go ahead.

148
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:55,200
The desk unit should be on its back, though.

149
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:55,900
Found it.

150
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:58,440
It's a 5-inch one!

151
00:08:58,440 --> 00:08:59,840
What is this?

152
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:01,500
It's a floppy disk.

153
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:04,680
Aren't floppy disks supposed to be smaller?

154
00:09:04,860 --> 00:09:08,540
About fifteen years ago,
that's what a floppy disk was.

155
00:09:08,540 --> 00:09:11,880
Yeah, when it was designed,
this was cutting-edge technology,

156
00:09:11,880 --> 00:09:15,240
but not anymore.
So what about a CD-ROM drive?

157
00:09:15,540 --> 00:09:16,400
It doesn't have one.

158
00:09:18,500 --> 00:09:20,680
Then how does it store maps and things?

159
00:09:21,300 --> 00:09:22,375
Rest assured.

160
00:09:22,425 --> 00:09:25,380
I can memorize everything I see,
exactly as it is.

161
00:09:25,660 --> 00:09:28,420
Doesn't that require
more advanced technology?

162
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:32,000
This robot is hard to figure out,
whether it's low-tech or high-tech.

163
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,380
It was completed properly.

164
00:09:41,880 --> 00:09:44,480
It finished 10 books,
500 pages' worth, in just three minutes.

165
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:47,340
With five billion yen spent on it,
it's only natural it can do that much.

166
00:09:47,980 --> 00:09:50,460
Right, go patrol the
route we just discussed.

167
00:09:50,460 --> 00:09:51,840
Understood.

168
00:09:57,020 --> 00:09:58,840
Finally got rid of that nuisance.

169
00:09:59,220 --> 00:10:00,680
I wonder if they'll be all right alone.

170
00:10:00,680 --> 00:10:04,480
It has to be able to handle patrol duty on its own,
or there's no point to it.

171
00:10:04,480 --> 00:10:07,520
Five billion yen went into that thing,
you know.

172
00:10:08,020 --> 00:10:09,540
But I still feel uneasy about it.

173
00:10:13,920 --> 00:10:15,140
Looks like it's fine.

174
00:10:15,740 --> 00:10:16,640
Watch out!

175
00:10:16,640 --> 00:10:18,320
Object approaching.

176
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:20,360
Calculating damage from the impact.

177
00:10:22,160 --> 00:10:23,120
Yes!

178
00:10:25,140 --> 00:10:26,080
Are you okay?

179
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:27,960
No abnormalities.

180
00:10:28,520 --> 00:10:29,520
Rear, clear.

181
00:10:29,520 --> 00:10:31,000
Left, clear.

182
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,400
Right, clear.

183
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:35,400
All circuits are normal.

184
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:37,220
It's amazingly sturdy.

185
00:10:37,220 --> 00:10:39,340
Sturdiness seems to be its only strength.

186
00:10:39,340 --> 00:10:40,520
Wait a minute.

187
00:10:41,880 --> 00:10:43,120
Looks like it could make friends.

188
00:10:47,260 --> 00:10:48,240
Ryotsu-dono!

189
00:10:48,780 --> 00:10:50,320
Well, Honda, what's going on?

190
00:10:50,860 --> 00:10:53,180
I came to see the robot police
officer everyone's talking about.

191
00:10:53,620 --> 00:10:56,420
He doesn't seem to be here.
Is he out on patrol?

192
00:10:56,820 --> 00:10:58,320
Well, you see, Ryo-chan...

193
00:10:58,740 --> 00:10:59,780
Sorry to keep you waiting.

194
00:10:59,780 --> 00:11:00,720
Here it comes.

195
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:02,200
Here's your curry rice.

196
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:05,580
W-what is this waiter?

197
00:11:05,580 --> 00:11:07,740
This is 001.

198
00:11:08,660 --> 00:11:11,640
Wasn't this supposed to be the police robot?

199
00:11:12,700 --> 00:11:17,660
This model's design is too old. There's no way it
can handle the complicated work of a police officer.

200
00:11:17,660 --> 00:11:21,580
So we're having it try out different
jobs to see what it's suited for.

201
00:11:22,860 --> 00:11:25,240
Until this morning,
I had a subway construction job.

202
00:11:25,780 --> 00:11:27,880
After that, I was handing out
tissues in front of the station.

203
00:11:27,880 --> 00:11:32,660
Yesterday I had him try waitressing at a family restaurant,
but the customers got creeped out and ran away.

204
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:35,060
He really does all sorts of things,
doesn't he?

205
00:11:35,420 --> 00:11:39,560
Well, it's my parental kindness, wanting
to put him to use for the good of society.

206
00:11:39,920 --> 00:11:42,560
But all the part-time pay goes to Ryo-chan,
doesn't it?

207
00:11:43,640 --> 00:11:44,800
It can't be helped.

208
00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:48,580
I'm diligently saving money
for this guy's retirement.

209
00:11:48,580 --> 00:11:50,560
Does a robot even have a retirement?

210
00:11:50,560 --> 00:11:52,160
Thank you for your patronage.

211
00:11:52,940 --> 00:11:54,660
That'll be 650 yen.

212
00:11:54,660 --> 00:11:56,000
Thanks for the meal.

213
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:58,340
Deduct it from your part-time pay.

214
00:11:58,340 --> 00:11:58,960
Hey.

215
00:11:59,620 --> 00:12:02,200
I've finished this plate,
so please take it away.

216
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:03,040
Hey.

217
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:08,140
You're using five billion robots just to suit your own needs,
completely.

218
00:12:08,140 --> 00:12:09,780
Yes, thank you for your business.

219
00:12:09,780 --> 00:12:13,440
Hey, wait, sorry, but could you give
me a little massage before you go?

220
00:12:13,440 --> 00:12:13,840
Yes.

221
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:15,900
You can do massages?

222
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:20,360
Three days ago, when we had you working at the sauna,
you seemed pretty skilled.

223
00:12:20,360 --> 00:12:22,140
Even that?

224
00:12:22,540 --> 00:12:25,100
Zero-zero-one-five,
put a little more strength into it.

225
00:12:25,100 --> 00:12:26,720
Yes, understood.

226
00:12:27,300 --> 00:12:29,000
That's good, more.

227
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:35,341
Ah ah ah ah ah ah

228
00:12:35,391 --> 00:12:39,044
Ah ah ah ah ah ah ah,

229
00:12:39,094 --> 00:12:42,723
Ah ah ah ah ah ah ah,

230
00:12:42,773 --> 00:12:46,452
Ah ah ah ah ah ah ah,

231
00:12:46,502 --> 00:12:50,118
Ah ah ah ah ah ah ah,

232
00:12:50,168 --> 00:12:53,835
Ah ah ah ah ah ah ah,

233
00:12:53,885 --> 00:12:57,526
Ah ah ah ah ah ah ah,

234
00:12:57,576 --> 00:13:01,400
Ah ah ah ah ah ah ah, ah

235
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:09,880
Repeating the same mistake,
you're worse than a robot.

236
00:13:12,940 --> 00:13:13,740
What? What is it?

237
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:15,062
Sir,

238
00:13:15,112 --> 00:13:20,480
Sir, you have to pay what you owe.
We can't have that going unpaid.

239
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:23,920
If you can't buy it,
leave the gourmet food behind.

240
00:13:23,920 --> 00:13:27,080
Right, the day before yesterday
it was doing debt collection work.

241
00:13:27,080 --> 00:13:29,860
What, you had it doing
that kind of thing too?

242
00:13:29,860 --> 00:13:33,960
Thank you for your business.
You'll be paying too, sir.

243
00:13:33,960 --> 00:13:34,860
Fine by me.

244
00:13:34,860 --> 00:13:36,240
If you can't pay,

245
00:13:36,240 --> 00:13:39,660
What are you doing?

246
00:13:41,680 --> 00:13:42,480
That hurts.

247
00:13:42,480 --> 00:13:46,060
It stopped.

248
00:13:46,060 --> 00:13:48,820
So that's where the switch is

249
00:13:48,820 --> 00:13:51,720
We were so close.

250
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:52,800
Senpai.

251
00:14:07,740 --> 00:14:09,940
This is totally overheated.

252
00:14:09,940 --> 00:14:11,680
It's because Ryo-chan works it to the bone.

253
00:14:11,680 --> 00:14:14,900
We only had it working for four
days straight without a break.

254
00:14:14,900 --> 00:14:17,340
According to this manual,

255
00:14:17,340 --> 00:14:21,460
it says to limit intense
activity to within one hour.

256
00:14:21,460 --> 00:14:22,220
What?

257
00:14:22,340 --> 00:14:25,360
Damn it, I thought its sturdiness
was its only good point.

258
00:14:25,360 --> 00:14:29,180
Being shock-resistant and being able to
run continuously are two different things.

259
00:14:29,860 --> 00:14:32,740
What are we going to do, Ryo-chan? If
the Chief finds out, we're in big trouble.

260
00:14:32,740 --> 00:14:33,880
Hmm...

261
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:38,440
Alright! It's a robot designed thirty years ago!
I'll show you how to fix it!

262
00:14:39,820 --> 00:14:43,160
Vacuum tubes! And so many of them!

263
00:14:43,160 --> 00:14:45,700
Thirty years ago, that would've been true.

264
00:14:45,700 --> 00:14:49,440
At this rate, getting parts will be the real problem,
before we even get to repairs.

265
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:56,560
No choice! Let's say Unit 001 was hit by a truck
while saving a child and died an honorable death.

266
00:14:56,560 --> 00:15:00,200
But it was totally fine when it got hit by a truck the other day,
wasn't it?

267
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:05,780
Then let's say it was trampled by a monster
while protecting the peace of the Earth.

268
00:15:05,780 --> 00:15:08,080
Who would believe a story like that?

269
00:15:08,080 --> 00:15:12,180
You never know. There are still many unknown creatures in the world,
you see.

270
00:15:12,180 --> 00:15:14,140
Senior, let's think of some other way.

271
00:15:14,140 --> 00:15:14,980
I see.

272
00:15:14,980 --> 00:15:16,960
Joe! Something terrible has happened!

273
00:15:16,960 --> 00:15:17,560
What is it?

274
00:15:17,560 --> 00:15:24,600
I just got word that the Chief and the others are
heading here with the Commissioner to inspect Unit 001.

275
00:15:29,260 --> 00:15:31,380
Sorry to trouble you,
Ohara, when you're injured.

276
00:15:31,380 --> 00:15:33,100
After all, today is an unofficial visit.

277
00:15:33,100 --> 00:15:34,660
Not at all, sir.

278
00:15:34,660 --> 00:15:36,420
For the sake of the station
chief or the Commissioner,

279
00:15:36,420 --> 00:15:37,900
please, Commissioner, this way.

280
00:15:37,900 --> 00:15:39,720
Thank you, Ohara.

281
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:41,020
Not at all.

282
00:15:41,960 --> 00:15:43,880
We've been expecting you, Commissioner.

283
00:15:43,880 --> 00:15:45,360
Good work.

284
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:47,000
Where's Ryotsu?

285
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,320
Senpai is out on patrol.

286
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:52,120
So that's the Traffic King

287
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:53,540
As for Unit 001,

288
00:15:54,480 --> 00:15:56,120
he's in the back writing a report.

289
00:15:56,560 --> 00:15:57,840
Good, call him over.

290
00:15:57,840 --> 00:16:00,920
Yes, 001,
the Commissioner is calling for you.

291
00:16:00,920 --> 00:16:03,760
How has Unit 001's work been?

292
00:16:03,760 --> 00:16:05,180
Well, that's...

293
00:16:05,180 --> 00:16:07,240
His work has been absolutely outstanding.

294
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:08,700
I see, I see.

295
00:16:08,700 --> 00:16:10,720
After all, it took 30 years.

296
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:13,280
Five billion yen has been poured into it,
after all.

297
00:16:13,280 --> 00:16:14,080
Sorry to keep you waiting.

298
00:16:17,320 --> 00:16:19,540
I am Unit 001.

299
00:16:19,540 --> 00:16:22,440
Commissioner, this is Unit 001.

300
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:25,060
This is the first time I've seen it moving.

301
00:16:26,560 --> 00:16:27,880
It seems to have shrunk, though.

302
00:16:27,880 --> 00:16:30,200
Moving and standing still are

303
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:31,680
quite different impressions.

304
00:16:31,680 --> 00:16:34,960
Besides, it's been on intense duty lately.

305
00:16:34,960 --> 00:16:36,760
Maybe its battery is running low.

306
00:16:36,760 --> 00:16:38,680
What? That's not good!

307
00:16:39,040 --> 00:16:41,320
Unit 001 took thirty years

308
00:16:41,320 --> 00:16:43,080
and five billion yen to build!

309
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:45,600
Hey, Terai,
get ready to charge it right away.

310
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:47,320
Charge it?

311
00:16:47,480 --> 00:16:48,220
But that's...

312
00:16:48,700 --> 00:16:50,540
What are you mumbling about?

313
00:16:50,540 --> 00:16:51,760
Charge it quickly!

314
00:16:51,760 --> 00:16:52,260
Yes.

315
00:16:54,020 --> 00:16:55,060
Ready, sir.

316
00:16:56,560 --> 00:17:06,880
It still has enough energy, so charging isn't necessary.
What a considerate robot for a machine! Terai, charge it up a lot anyway.

317
00:17:08,520 --> 00:17:13,760
What are you dawdling for? Hurry up and do it.
Yes. You two are excused.

318
00:17:21,820 --> 00:17:32,420
Nooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooo!

319
00:17:32,420 --> 00:17:35,500
Considering it took 30 years
and 5 billion yen to build,

320
00:17:35,500 --> 00:17:38,940
you sure react dynamically
just to get charged.

321
00:17:38,940 --> 00:17:39,700
I see.

322
00:17:39,700 --> 00:17:41,288
Dry-gu,

323
00:17:41,338 --> 00:17:45,600
that's enough of that, surely.

324
00:17:48,160 --> 00:17:49,440
Are you okay, 0015?

325
00:17:51,240 --> 00:17:53,880
Of course I'm not okay, you idiot!

326
00:17:53,880 --> 00:17:56,020
You nearly got electrocuted there!

327
00:17:56,020 --> 00:17:58,180
So, now that it's charged,

328
00:17:58,180 --> 00:18:00,420
let's have this unhooked.

329
00:18:02,700 --> 00:18:06,220
With you, ten seconds should
be enough to solve it, right?

330
00:18:06,220 --> 00:18:07,340
What's that?

331
00:18:07,340 --> 00:18:10,520
Here's a problem worthy of
a Nobel Prize in Physics.

332
00:18:11,220 --> 00:18:11,580
This is

333
00:18:12,760 --> 00:18:13,900
Can it do it?

334
00:18:14,680 --> 00:18:18,680
Of course, it's only natural that
we ordinary folks have no idea.

335
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:21,220
But isn't it taking a bit too long?

336
00:18:21,220 --> 00:18:24,420
Yes... maybe it doesn't have enough charge?

337
00:18:24,420 --> 00:18:25,020
I see.

338
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:28,120
Right, Terai, charge it right away.

339
00:18:28,480 --> 00:18:28,840
Yes.

340
00:18:35,120 --> 00:18:37,560
No, no, harder!

341
00:18:39,440 --> 00:18:43,240
Robot 001, are you all right?

342
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:45,220
1000...0015?

343
00:18:45,480 --> 00:18:47,460
I-I-I did it!

344
00:18:48,160 --> 00:18:51,840
W-what is this?

345
00:18:51,840 --> 00:18:53,400
What's going on here?

346
00:18:53,400 --> 00:18:55,920
According to this manual...

347
00:18:55,920 --> 00:18:59,480
it says the calculation circuit
malfunctions right after charging.

348
00:18:59,480 --> 00:19:02,480
But the Commissioner has come all this way.

349
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:06,460
Well, even if the calculations are bad, we
can still test its physical abilities, right?

350
00:19:06,460 --> 00:19:07,340
Right.

351
00:19:08,180 --> 00:19:10,640
I see. So shall we test
it outside this time?

352
00:19:10,640 --> 00:19:10,960
Yeah.

353
00:19:11,700 --> 00:19:14,560
Alright, now it's a physical
fitness test at the park out front!

354
00:19:15,520 --> 00:19:19,080
The scenario is that a truck
fell apart at the intersection.

355
00:19:19,080 --> 00:19:20,840
Get started on restoring it right away.

356
00:19:20,840 --> 00:19:22,280
Me alone?

357
00:19:22,280 --> 00:19:24,880
Of course. Alright, let's get to work!

358
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:27,320
Damn it, I'm going all out!

359
00:19:31,380 --> 00:19:32,900
Impressive as always!

360
00:19:33,100 --> 00:19:37,040
It's taken thirty years and
five billion yen to develop.

361
00:19:38,820 --> 00:19:40,920
Looks like the ace is getting slow.

362
00:19:40,920 --> 00:19:42,380
Ohara, what's the matter?

363
00:19:42,700 --> 00:19:45,840
Yes, maybe the power's running low again.

364
00:19:45,840 --> 00:19:47,180
I see. Yes, I suppose so.

365
00:19:58,800 --> 00:19:59,920
Finished.

366
00:20:01,280 --> 00:20:02,580
It's juice.

367
00:20:03,140 --> 00:20:03,500
Thank you.

368
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:07,120
But even though it's a robot, the
"JJ" thing...

369
00:20:07,120 --> 00:20:10,880
It's built to be that close to a human.

370
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:13,180
What kind of test are you doing next?

371
00:20:13,740 --> 00:20:17,840
Next, we'll test it underwater, so I'm
thinking of going to the river nearby.

372
00:20:18,660 --> 00:20:20,860
I see, that sounds like fun.

373
00:20:21,480 --> 00:20:25,500
Don't joke around. If I'm made to do anything more,
I'll drop dead.

374
00:20:25,920 --> 00:20:27,720
Anyway, my throat is so dry.

375
00:20:28,920 --> 00:20:29,320
Right.

376
00:20:30,720 --> 00:20:32,140
There's a UFO outside the window!

377
00:20:32,840 --> 00:20:33,800
Where?

378
00:20:33,800 --> 00:20:35,240
Where, where?

379
00:20:35,240 --> 00:20:37,500
0015, where's the UFO?

380
00:20:38,940 --> 00:20:42,960
Ohara-kun, I think we just saw
something we shouldn't have seen...

381
00:20:42,960 --> 00:20:44,580
Yes, me too.

382
00:20:44,580 --> 00:20:46,500
I don't see it anywhere.

383
00:20:46,500 --> 00:20:48,160
Now it's over to the right.

384
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:48,760
Where?

385
00:20:51,720 --> 00:20:52,520
Nice.

386
00:20:52,520 --> 00:20:54,500
You've really done it now.

387
00:20:56,100 --> 00:20:58,040
I am Robot 001.

388
00:20:58,040 --> 00:20:59,520
Your face is backwards.

389
00:20:59,520 --> 00:21:00,160
Clunk!

390
00:21:00,260 --> 00:21:00,680
Heh heh.

391
00:21:00,680 --> 00:21:02,420
Where's Robot 001?

392
00:21:02,580 --> 00:21:04,660
I am Robot 001.

393
00:21:04,660 --> 00:21:07,640
So you insist you're not Ryotsu, after all.

394
00:21:07,640 --> 00:21:08,740
Y-yes, that's right.

395
00:21:09,540 --> 00:21:09,980
Yes.

396
00:21:09,980 --> 00:21:12,520
The temple nearby is on fire?

397
00:21:17,580 --> 00:21:18,980
Where's the fire truck?

398
00:21:19,360 --> 00:21:21,540
It looks like it's stuck in traffic.

399
00:21:21,540 --> 00:21:23,120
P-Please do something!

400
00:21:23,120 --> 00:21:25,520
The temple has a treasure
passed down for over 300 years,

401
00:21:25,920 --> 00:21:29,000
a precious Buddhist statue
that weighs 200 kilograms!

402
00:21:29,900 --> 00:21:32,880
It's all right.
Head priest, please don't worry.

403
00:21:33,080 --> 00:21:36,620
We have a wonderful robot
officer for times like this.

404
00:21:36,740 --> 00:21:37,640
Hey, Chief.

405
00:21:37,880 --> 00:21:39,500
Right, right. Ohare-kun.

406
00:21:39,780 --> 00:21:40,180
Yes!

407
00:21:41,660 --> 00:21:43,700
Hey! 001, it's your turn.

408
00:21:43,880 --> 00:21:47,200
I'm already overworked today,
and my body isn't in good shape...

409
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:48,780
What!? I see!

410
00:21:49,420 --> 00:21:53,420
It says 001 will dive
into the fire on its own.

411
00:21:53,420 --> 00:21:55,500
Right, come on, let's go.

412
00:21:56,840 --> 00:21:58,340
Doesn't it seem reluctant?

413
00:21:58,560 --> 00:22:01,820
No, it's just that it's so modest
by nature that it's embarrassed.

414
00:22:01,820 --> 00:22:02,360
I see.

415
00:22:03,100 --> 00:22:04,660
Ryotsu, give up.

416
00:22:04,660 --> 00:22:07,720
If we can save this national
treasure-level Buddhist statue...

417
00:22:07,720 --> 00:22:11,440
We might be able to overlook
a little of Unit 001's flaws.

418
00:22:11,440 --> 00:22:12,280
A little?

419
00:22:12,660 --> 00:22:15,240
That's right,
it might at least save its life.

420
00:22:15,240 --> 00:22:16,180
Come on!

421
00:22:18,220 --> 00:22:19,240
Ryo-chan.

422
00:22:19,240 --> 00:22:22,140
Looks like the secret about Unit 001 got out

423
00:22:23,420 --> 00:22:26,320
Since it's Senpai we're talking about,
I think he'll manage somehow.

424
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:30,340
Ohane-kun, is Unit 001 all right?

425
00:22:30,760 --> 00:22:33,020
It's fine. That guy is immortal.

426
00:22:33,020 --> 00:22:36,860
After all,
it took 30 years and 5 billion yen.

427
00:22:36,860 --> 00:22:38,460
Right. That's true.

428
00:22:51,020 --> 00:22:53,000
Well, what excellent performance.

429
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:55,720
With this, we can entrust it
with missions without worry.

430
00:22:55,720 --> 00:22:57,460
Regarding the mission?

431
00:22:57,460 --> 00:23:00,520
Actually, with the cooperation of police
forces from various countries and NASA,

432
00:23:00,520 --> 00:23:03,500
we're going to set up a police
organization on a global scale.

433
00:23:03,500 --> 00:23:07,060
I understand the police forces of various countries,
but what about NASA?

434
00:23:07,060 --> 00:23:10,400
Yes, it's a space police box
using artificial satellites.

435
00:23:11,800 --> 00:23:13,060
So you'll be stationed there.

436
00:23:13,060 --> 00:23:14,940
A space police box.

437
00:23:14,940 --> 00:23:17,040
Alright, departure right now!

438
00:23:17,040 --> 00:23:20,020
Wait, the truth is, I'm a human being!

439
00:23:20,020 --> 00:23:20,900
Hey, you!

440
00:23:20,900 --> 00:23:22,920
It won't come off.

441
00:23:23,720 --> 00:23:25,700
Applying heat suddenly,

442
00:23:25,700 --> 00:23:28,560
and then cooling it in water,
it's become stuck and won't come off.

443
00:23:29,760 --> 00:23:34,080
Just as expected from 30
years and 5 billion rejections,

444
00:23:34,080 --> 00:23:35,960
its jokes are as good as a human's.

445
00:23:35,960 --> 00:23:37,840
Come on, hurry up, 0015!

446
00:23:37,840 --> 00:23:40,220
I'm not joking, really.

447
00:23:41,800 --> 00:23:45,214
Wait! I'm human! Bu-

448
00:23:45,264 --> 00:23:46,080
Bucha!

449
00:23:50,100 --> 00:23:56,820
T-this can't be happening!

450
00:23:56,820 --> 00:23:58,420
Aaaaaaah!

451
00:23:58,420 --> 00:24:01,240
Eeeeeeeh!

452
00:24:02,300 --> 00:24:03,180
Eeeeeeeh!

453
00:24:03,180 --> 00:24:03,640
Eeeeeeeh!

454
00:24:03,640 --> 00:24:04,620
Eeeeeeeh!

455
00:24:10,540 --> 00:24:14,460
Amid the seasons that pass by,
reflected sadly

456
00:24:14,460 --> 00:24:16,000
Eeeeeee

457
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:19,300
I've gotten good at forced smiles

458
00:24:19,640 --> 00:24:20,880
Eeeeeee

459
00:24:20,880 --> 00:24:24,680
Drifting along and changing, I am to you

460
00:24:24,680 --> 00:24:29,120
I wonder how I appear to others

461
00:24:30,600 --> 00:24:36,040
After our fights,
we always share a brief kiss

462
00:24:36,040 --> 00:24:40,100
I loved you with your teary eyes

463
00:24:40,100 --> 00:24:45,360
Such irreplaceable things,

464
00:24:45,860 --> 00:24:50,800
I wonder how many a
person holds in a lifetime

465
00:24:52,520 --> 00:24:57,160
You are me, and I am you

466
00:24:58,220 --> 00:25:02,200
That alone was enough to make me whole

467
00:25:03,080 --> 00:25:08,280
Just from you smiling

468
00:25:08,640 --> 00:25:14,920
I felt like every pain was healed

469
00:25:21,240 --> 00:25:23,200
They said he was a world-famous violinist

470
00:25:23,200 --> 00:25:24,860
so I wondered what kind of man he'd be

471
00:25:24,860 --> 00:25:26,940
but he's just a cheerful foreign old guy

472
00:25:26,940 --> 00:25:29,360
The violin's gone?

473
00:25:29,780 --> 00:25:31,540
That Stradivarius...

474
00:25:31,540 --> 00:25:33,400
is it really that amazing of a violin?

475
00:25:33,960 --> 00:25:36,100
Next time: The Great Stradivarius Chase

476
00:25:36,480 --> 00:25:37,100
See you then

